\pard\b\f0\fs24 John Walker\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Ethnicity:\b0\f1  Greek, American.\par
\b\f0 Position:\b0\f1  Captain, Protectant field commander.\par
\b\f0 Age:\b0\f1  34.\par
\b\f0 Sex:\b0\f1  Male.\par
\b\f0 Height:\b0\f1  183 cm.\par
\b\f0 Build:\b0\f1  Athletic.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  Primary protagonist. John leads the lost-facility mission, becomes the first major human-sentient bridge through the HMNI transformation, and carries the moral centre of the story.\par
\b\f0 Goal:\b0\f1  Keep his squad alive, uncover the truth behind the lost facility, and find a path that preserves life without surrendering human agency.\par
\b\f0 Physical Description:\b0\f1  Moderately tall, athletic and chiseled. Life on Ceres has left his legs leaner than they would be under full gravity. His uniform is often a little untidy, but his field kit is always exact.\par
\b\f0 Personality:\b0\f1  Calm, compassionate, quietly funny, deeply observant, and hard to rattle under pressure. A natural leader who values trust over rank theatre.\par
\b\f0 Occupation:\b0\f1  Captain within the Protectant. Roughly 20 years of service. Also trains recruits in deep-space operations.\par
\b\f0 Habits/Mannerisms:\b0\f1  Checks gear obsessively. Speaks softly even under stress. Dislikes forced salutes and prefers genuine camaraderie. Becomes colder only when the mission demands it.\par
\b\f0 Background:\b0\f1  Raised around horses and farm life before joining Protectant training at 17. Based on Ceres, he was preparing for Europa when Marcellus redirected him toward the hidden facility in Nepal.\par
\b\f0 Internal Conflicts:\b0\f1  Struggles with estrangement from his mother, distrust of rigid command structures, and the fear of losing his humanity after becoming a hybrid.\par
\b\f0 External Conflicts:\b0\f1  Marcellus uses him as a tool while hiding the truth. John is caught between Protectant doctrine and the Sentient vision of the future.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  His hybrid body lets him perceive data, energy and systems in ways baseline humans cannot, making him central to any future human-sentient rapprochement.\par
}
